; Entity handler: Death flying right (room 18)
;
; Death, the flying reaper of room 18 (Banquet of Death), during the half of its patrol in which it moves right (the
; other half is #R$BA15). Entity handlers are not called: the slot walker #R$A5E9 sets SP to a slot of #R$C100 and
; RETs, so the handler is entered with SP at slot+2 (the handler word has been popped) and finds its state on the
; stack. It pops the words it needs, pushes back the ones that changed, and ends by jumping to #R$A5F0 with HL at the
; next slot (here through #R$B41F).
; .
; State used by this half, from the slot (#R$C100): +2 word speed (signed 8.8, 2-pixel units per frame), +4 byte left
; turning point, +5 byte right turning point, +6 word x (8.8; the high byte is in 2-pixel units). The speed is added
; to x; when the high byte of x equals the right turning point the handler word of the slot is rewritten with #R$BA15,
; so that from the next frame on the same speed is subtracted. Both halves go on at #R$BA32. IY is the address the
; animation code at #R$BA79 jumps to when it has chosen the graphics: $B3D2 takes the second of the two frame tables
; of the sprite block (#R$B3D2 skips the first), which is the table for this direction; #R$BA15 uses $B3D4, the first
; table.
;
; SP Slot address + 2 (the handler word was popped by the RET that entered the routine)
@label=UpdateDeathRight
c$B9F8 LD IY,$B3D2   ; frame table for moving right (the second one)
 $B9FC POP BC        ; speed
 $B9FD POP DE        ; D right turning point, E left turning point
 $B9FE POP HL        ; x (8.8)
 $B9FF ADD HL,BC     ; x moves right
 $BA00 PUSH HL       ; store x
 $BA01 POP HL        ; SP is back at +8
 $BA02 LD A,H        ; x in 2-pixel units
 $BA03 CP D          ; at the right turning point?
 $BA04 JR NZ,$BA32   ;
 $BA06 LD HL,$FFFA   ; -6: back to slot+2
 $BA09 ADD HL,SP     ;
 $BA0A LD SP,HL      ;
 $BA0B LD HL,$BA15   ; next frame this slot is handled by the moving-left half
 $BA0E PUSH HL       ; written over the handler word at slot+0
 $BA0F POP HL        ;
 $BA10 POP BC        ; pop speed, limits and x again
 $BA11 POP DE        ;
 $BA12 POP HL        ;
 $BA13 JR $BA32      ;
